From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Writer lists body paragraphs without exporting the document

- ElyDoc read the body by saving a flat ODF copy. ODF export hides
  tracked deletions for its length and shows them again, so a read
  took seconds with thousands of changes and pushed a cursor out of
  deleted text (R23.2b).
- getCommandValues(".uno:ElyBody") lists each body paragraph with its
  style's programmatic name and its text: fields expanded; footnote,
  comment and frame anchors and tracked deletions left out, also a
  deletion under a format change, which HideDeletions misses. A
  deleted paragraph break joins the two paragraphs, and a
  paragraph deleted from its start takes the next one's style, as
  the flat export does. Nothing in the document or the view changes.

